      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/ezwebtools/flowpick\n\n### Category\n\nOther\n\n### Project Title\n\nFlowPick\n\n### Project Description\n\nFlowPick is an open-source browser extension for finding and downloading media from web pages.\n\nIt captures media requests directly from your browser session, so it can find resources that aren't always visible in the page source, including dynamically loaded content and media behind a logged-in session.\n\nIt supports HLS/M3U8, DASH/MPD, MP4, WebM, audio files, and images. You can preview and filter detected resources, batch download files, and handle some stream merging directly in the browser.\n\nFlowPick is useful for downloading videos, saving images in bulk, collecting media assets, inspecting stream requests, and general web development work.\n\nMost processing happens locally in the browser, so files don't need to be uploaded to another server.\n\nBuilt with TypeScript and WebExtension APIs. Available for Chrome, Edge, Firefox, and other Chromium-based browsers.\n\n### Highlights\n\nUnlike URL-based downloaders, FlowPick detects media requests directly from the active browser session. This means it can find dynamically loaded media and work with pages you're already logged into. It also handles HLS/M3U8, DASH/MPD, video, audio, and images in one extension, with most processing done locally.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```markdown\n\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n<img width=\"1128\" height=\"697\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c426d11-f0f7-4942-b042-e69e49c8eeb5\" />\n<img width=\"1240\" height=\"771\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cf66ff6-83ab-4fc5-b1b9-6a993ba51981\" />\n<img width=\"1117\" height=\"703\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6bf3a7d0-df19-484e-98ff-eaf53f7d11c3\" />",
